# evolution-data-server -- the calendar and contacts backend, and the reason it
# is in a desktop bring-up at all: gnome-shell links libedataserver and libecal
# UNCONDITIONALLY (gnome-shell meson.build:72-73). There is no shell without it.
#
# GNOME 48 series, BLFS 12.4.
SRC_URL=https://download.gnome.org/sources/evolution-data-server/3.56/evolution-data-server-3.56.2.tar.xz
SRC_SHA256=df4ec29950f29a76eac6fbe0f814c48d2cef7d3fdb905002a4a883dd761ce93c
SRC_DIR=evolution-data-server-3.56.2

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE DOCUMENTED ESCAPE HATCH FROM NSS DOES NOT WORK. DO NOT RETRY IT.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# cmake/modules/FindSMIME.cmake opens by documenting -DENABLE_SMIME=OFF as the
# way to skip NSS. The option IS honoured -- for the CODE, through config.h and
# #ifdef blocks in src/camel. It is NEVER CONSULTED BY THE SEARCH: the module
# runs pkg-config for nspr/nss unconditionally, then falls through to a manual
# hunt that ends in FATAL_ERROR.
#
# The flag disables the feature and not the requirement. Upstream has known
# since bug 792746, "Fails to build with ENABLE_SMIME set to OFF". This is
# recorded here so nobody spends an evening on it believing the header comment,
# which is why nspr and nss are packaged at all.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# -DENABLE_INTROSPECTION=ON, BECAUSE THE DEFAULT IS **OFF**
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# cmake/modules/GObjectIntrospection.cmake:16 is
# `add_printable_option(ENABLE_INTROSPECTION "..." OFF)`.
#
# The `-DENABLE_INTROSPECTION=ON` visible near the top of CMakeLists.txt (line
# 31) is INSIDE THE FILE'S COMMENT HEADER -- a worked example of how to
# configure, not code. Reading only that would give exactly the wrong answer.
#
# Left alone, e-d-s builds, installs every library, and ships NO TYPELIBS, and
# nothing in the build says so. Same shape as libjxl's plugins default: the
# option that carries the point of the package is the one that is off.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TWO INSTALL PATHS THAT ARE WRONG BY DEFAULT AND SILENT ABOUT IT
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# -DSYSCONF_INSTALL_DIR=/etc. CMakeLists.txt:183 defaults it to
# ${CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX}/etc -- i.e. /usr/etc, which nothing on this system
# reads. e-d-s does NOT use GNUInstallDirs, so this is not the lib64 problem
# _scripts/build-cmake.sh already handles; CMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDIR is simply
# ignored here. LIB_INSTALL_DIR lands correctly at /usr/lib only because
# LIB_SUFFIX defaults to empty (CMakeLists.txt:159, 177) -- right answer,
# different mechanism, so it is stated rather than assumed.
#
# -DWITH_SYSTEMDUSERUNITDIR=no. Defaults to ${CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX}/lib/systemd/
# user (CMakeLists.txt:248) and installs four user units unconditionally. Duct
# has elogind and NO systemd user session for a unit to be installed into --
# same reasoning dconf's pkg.env already records. Nothing is lost: the D-Bus
# activation files install UNCONDITIONALLY to /usr/share/dbus-1/services
# regardless of this setting, and D-Bus activation is what actually starts these
# four services. With units off, the SystemdService= line is correctly omitted
# from those files (src/services/*/CMakeLists.txt:1-13).
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# -DWITH_LIBDB=OFF IS MANDATORY, NOT TIDYING
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# It defaults to ON (CMakeLists.txt:516) and, when it cannot compile against
# db.h, raises FATAL_ERROR (:546). Berkeley DB is not packaged in this tree, so
# leaving this alone stops the configure dead.
#
# Turning it off costs nothing real. Its ONLY use is migrating a pre-existing
# Berkeley DB addressbook to sqlite -- src/addressbook/backends/file/
# e-book-backend-file.c:2343, "The old BDB exists, lets migrate that to sqlite
# right away", gated on an addressbook.db that cannot exist on a first install.
#
# It does change libebackend: e-dbhash.c and e-db3-utils.c drop out along with
# their public headers (src/libebackend/CMakeLists.txt:65-74). Nothing this tree
# builds uses them. Flagged because it is an ABI difference, not just a feature.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The toolkits, and what turning them off actually removes
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# -DENABLE_GTK=OFF -DENABLE_GTK4=OFF. Both default ON, and each one enables a
# WebKit OAuth2 option that ALSO defaults ON and is a hard requirement:
# ENABLE_OAUTH2_WEBKITGTK wants webkit2gtk-4.1 and ENABLE_OAUTH2_WEBKITGTK4
# wants webkitgtk-6.0 (CMakeLists.txt:425-443). Neither WebKit is packaged, and
# neither is a small thing to package. Turning the toolkits off removes both
# requirements BY CONSTRUCTION -- the options are nested inside the toolkit
# blocks and are never even declared.
#
# What is lost, named rather than defaulted away: HAVE_GTK gates
# evolution-alarm-notify and evolution-user-prompter
# (src/services/CMakeLists.txt:5-8). Both are Evolution-application services.
# The shell needs neither; the shell needs libedataserver and libecal. The cost
# is that a backend needing to ask the user something -- an untrusted TLS
# certificate, most likely -- has no prompter to ask through, and fails instead.
# Acceptable for a desktop with no mail client packaged, and it should be
# revisited the day Evolution itself is.
#
# -DENABLE_CANBERRA=OFF. This one changed on reading rather than on assumption.
# It defaults ON and hard-requires libcanberra-gtk3 (CMakeLists.txt:801-806) --
# which this tree DOES have, so leaving it on would have worked. But its only
# consumer is src/services/evolution-alarm-notify, which ENABLE_GTK=OFF already
# excludes from the build. On would mean a hard dependency for a component that
# does not exist.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Off because the thing they need is not in the tree
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# -DENABLE_GOA=OFF: defaults ON, hard-requires goa-1.0 (:499-505).
# gnome-online-accounts belongs to another chain and is not published.
# -DENABLE_WEATHER=OFF: defaults ON, hard-requires gweather4 (:785-794), and
# libgweather is not packaged. It carries a second trap for whoever turns it
# back on -- a FATAL_ERROR unless gweather4's soupapiversion is exactly "3.0".
# -DWITH_KRB5=OFF: MANDATORY, and this comment previously said otherwise.
#
# It first claimed the default was a harmless probe -- "finding nothing is NOT an
# error" -- from reading FindKRB5.cmake:20-46 and stopping there. The module goes
# on to :117-123:
#
#     if(HAVE_KRB5) ... else() message(FATAL_ERROR "Failed to find Kerberos 5
#         libraries. Use -DWITH_KRB5=OFF to disable Kerberos 5 support")
#
# and that block is reached whenever WITH_KRB5 is truthy -- the early return at
# :20 fires only when it is FALSE. So the default is a hard failure without
# krb5, which is not packaged. The flag was right and the reason recorded for it
# was wrong; it was doing load-bearing work while described as tidiness.
#
# -DWITH_OPENLDAP=OFF: defaults to "ON" and raises FATAL_ERROR when OpenLDAP is
# absent (cmake/modules/FindLDAP.cmake:23, :95, :136). OpenLDAP is not packaged.
#
# THIS ONE IS HERE BECAUSE CI CAUGHT IT, AND THE MISS WAS IN MY SCAN, NOT IN THE
# BUILD FILE. The first pass grepped CMakeLists.txt for FATAL_ERROR but searched
# cmake/modules/ only for the words 'openldap|krb5|kerberos', through `head -10`
# -- and FindKRB5 sorts before FindLDAP, so the truncation ate the answer. A
# truncated search reads exactly like a complete one. The scan was redone over
# every FATAL_ERROR and every add_printable_* default in cmake/modules/ with no
# pipe to head, which is what found the next entry as well.
#
# -DENABLE_SCHEMAS_COMPILE=OFF: defaults ON (GLibTools.cmake:201) and is NOT a
# feature -- it appends install code that runs
#
#     cmake -E copy_if_different <schema> ${SHARE_INSTALL_PREFIX}/glib-2.0/schemas/
#
# to an ABSOLUTE path with NO DESTDIR PREFIX, then compiles there. So it writes
# into the build container's live /usr/share rather than into the staging root:
# it cannot contribute the compiled cache to this package, and it makes the
# install step non-hermetic. The README already assigns this job to the image
# build -- "tape has no install hooks", with glib-compile-schemas listed among
# the caches generated once over the whole installation.
#
# -DENABLE_EXAMPLES=OFF and -DENABLE_TESTS=OFF: both default ON and build
# programs that are not installed.
# -DENABLE_INSTALLED_TESTS=OFF: already OFF (cmake/modules/InstalledTests.cmake
# :20), pinned because CMakeLists.txt:294 makes it FATAL in combination with
# ENABLE_TESTS=OFF. Pinning both halves means the pair cannot be broken by an
# upstream default flipping under us.
#
# NOT SET, deliberately:
#
#   ENABLE_VALA_BINDINGS   already OFF (:989), and it is self-guarding: :993
#                          raises FATAL_ERROR if it is on without introspection.
#   ENABLE_BACKEND_PER_PROCESS  already OFF (:511); changes the process model,
#                          which is not something to alter during bring-up.
#   ENABLE_IPV6            left ON, its default. The check is a compile test for
#                          system interfaces (:732-765), not a package.
#   ENABLE_DOT_LOCKING     left ON, its default; mail spool locking, no
#                          dependency.
#   WITH_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID and the Outlook/Yahoo pairs: left empty. They embed
#                          OAuth2 application credentials, which are not ours to
#                          supply.
CMAKE_ARGS="-DSYSCONF_INSTALL_DIR=/etc \
-DWITH_SYSTEMDUSERUNITDIR=no \
-DENABLE_INTROSPECTION=ON \
-DWITH_LIBDB=OFF \
-DWITH_KRB5=OFF \
-DWITH_OPENLDAP=OFF \
-DENABLE_SCHEMAS_COMPILE=OFF \
-DENABLE_GTK=OFF \
-DENABLE_GTK4=OFF \
-DENABLE_CANBERRA=OFF \
-DENABLE_GOA=OFF \
-DENABLE_WEATHER=OFF \
-DENABLE_EXAMPLES=OFF \
-DENABLE_TESTS=OFF \
-DENABLE_INSTALLED_TESTS=OFF"
